<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">451 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">451 CE in world history: 8 events and 1 death. 160 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/410">410 CE</a><a href="/years/420">420 CE</a><a href="/years/429">429 CE</a><a href="/years/439">439 CE</a><a href="/years/451" aria-current="page">451 CE</a><a href="/years/454">454 CE</a><a href="/years/476">476 CE</a><a href="/years/533">533 CE</a><a href="/years/534">534 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-20">20 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Aetius checks Attila at the Catalaunian Plains</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A coalition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flavius-aetius">Aetius</a> fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> to a halt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, on a date traditionally given as 20 June. Attila withdrew, and invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> the following year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-8">8 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Council of Chalcedon opens</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishops</a> summoned by Emperor Marcian met at Chalcedon, across the Bosporus from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. Its definition of Christ as one person in two natures became orthodoxy in the West and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> but split the eastern churches.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-catalaunian-plains">Battle of the Catalaunian Plains</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of the Catalaunian Plains was fought in 451 in north-eastern Gaul between the Hunnic army of Attila and a coalition led by the Roman general Aetius and the Visigothic king Theodoric I.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-avarayr" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-avarayr.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-avarayr">Battle of Avarayr</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Avarayr was fought in 451 on the Avarayr plain, south-east of Lake Van in the historical province of Vaspurakan, between Armenian rebels led by Vardan Mamikonian and the army of the Sasanian king Yazdegerd II, who sought to impose Zoroastrianism.</p></div></li></ol></section>
